From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:13:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 222/342] dwc2: a high speed isochronous packet is armed only
 in the microframe before its own

Armed two microframes ahead (in one of its parity) the channel ran in
that microframe, too late to finish: a webcam microphone's packets had
22% frame overruns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.h               |  5 ++---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp | 14 +++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.h b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.h
index 2ac0d40b52..61c4355e8a 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.h
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.h
@@ -95,9 +95,8 @@ struct dwc2_iso_statistics {
 	channel for the frame's packet and its start-split parts (and
 	complete-splits, IN) follow from the channel's halt interrupt; or of a
 	high speed device (kIsoFirstHighSpeedStream on), a packet every
-	2^(bInterval-1) microframes, armed from the halt of the one before
-	(every microframe or every other one) or by the timer in the microframe
-	before its own.
+	2^(bInterval-1) microframes, armed in the microframe before its own:
+	from the halt of the one before (every microframe) or by the timer.
 	State changes under DWC2::fIsoLock.
 */
 struct dwc2_iso_stream {
diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp
index 0217ef0d1c..279c8b32ea 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp
@@ -38,10 +38,11 @@
  * wMaxPacketSize times the endpoint's transactions per microframe (1 to 3,
  * "high bandwidth"). The channel runs all of a microframe's transactions
  * from one enable (HCCHAR.MC, PKTCNT; IN starts at DATA0, DATA1 or DATA2
- * for 1, 2 or 3) and halts when they are done. Each packet is armed from
- * the halt of the one before (ODDFRM: the parity of its microframe) when
- * its microframe is at most two away; otherwise the timer arms it in the
- * microframe before, as for full speed. A microframe the stream could not
+ * for 1, 2 or 3) and halts when they are done. Each packet is armed in the
+ * microframe before its own (ODDFRM: its parity): from the halt of the one
+ * before when that is the next microframe, otherwise by the timer, as for
+ * full speed. (Armed in a microframe of its own parity, the channel may run
+ * in that one, too late to finish: a frame overrun.) A microframe the stream could not
  * catch is counted as missed, and the stream goes on from the next one.
  * HS isochronous OUT is not done yet.
  */
@@ -536,7 +537,10 @@ DWC2::_IsoStartHighSpeed(dwc2_iso_stream* stream)
 			frame = (now + 1) & 0x3fff;
 			ahead = 1;
 		}
-		if (ahead > 2) {
+		if (ahead > 1) {
+			// armed in a microframe of the packet's parity, the channel may
+			// run in that one, too late to finish (frame overrun): only in
+			// the microframe before
 			stream->pendingFrame = frame;
 			_IsoScheduleFrameTimer(stream, ahead);
 			return;
